We have a DILOG SCSI controller in our 5400. We have 3 WREN V's and 1 WREN
7 working just fine. Our disks are differential SCSI, the RZ57 is probably
single-ended. The DILOG controller is supposed to be switch selectable
between differential and single-ended. We have never (intentionally) tried
the single-ended configuration. We did forget to spec a differential WREN
7 and the result was very useful :).

We don't recommend our local DILOG salesleaze or installation people. In
fact, we did the installation after the installation tech said," Ultrix,
Unix, only speak VMS", and gave up. Anyway, the hardware works.

