This may sound like a dumb question, but I haven't done this before in
this particular environment.  I started a full backup onto TK50s of a
/usr filesystem on a MicroVAX-II running Ultrix 3.0.  When it asked for
a second tape, I inserted it, waited until it was on-line and typed
"yes" to the dump program.  Rather than immediately proceeding to write
on the second tape, the program simply ran and ran, chalking up CPU
time without touching the tape.  There was no doubt about my typing the
"yes" and the program no longer waiting for terminal input.  Since I
